			<div class="content" id="post-content-2298020">
									

<p>Thanks for explaining your vote. I'll admit it, that was something I struggled with, too, with this. I wanted to explore the Masquerade implications further, but it changed the quick-punch feel of the story. In the end, yes, I stuck to weird and disgusting. For this tale, it felt right to end it at the end of the video, which limited the reaction time.</p>
<p>However, I'd gladly write a follow-up that goes into the procedure behind how the SCP deals with a viral video threat and tracks down a new anomaly. There's a lot of interesting meat, there. Lots of rushing around that doesn't have to end in gunfights. I think that would be really fascinating.</p>

